   1. Tell me about Bootstrap 
     Answer (memorize this line): 
Bootstrap is a front-end framework used to build responsive and mobile-first websites 
quickly using pre-defined CSS and JavaScript components. 
 
   2. Why do you use Bootstrap? 
     Answer: 
It reduces development time and helps create responsive UI without writing CSS from 
scratch. 
 
   3. What is Grid System?   (VERY IMPORTANT) 
     Answer: 
Bootstrap uses a 12-column grid system to design layouts. We divide the screen into 12 
columns and assign width using col classes. 
     Example: 
<div class="row"> 
  <div class="col-4"></div> 
  <div class="col-8"></div> 
</div> 
     say: “4 + 8 = 12 columns” 
 
   4. What are containers? 
     Answer: 
Containers are used to wrap content. 
• .container → fixed width 
• .container-fluid → full width 
 
   5. What are breakpoints? 
     Answer: 
Breakpoints are screen sizes used to make the layout responsive. 
     Example: 
• sm 
• md 
• lg 
 
   6. Difference between col and col-md-6 
     Answer: 
col takes equal width, while col-md-6 takes 6 columns on medium screens. 
 
   7. What is Flexbox in Bootstrap? 
     Answer: 
Bootstrap uses flexbox for layout and alignment using classes like d-flex. 
 
   8. How to center a div?   (MOST ASKED) 
     Answer: 
d-flex justify-content-center align-items-center 
     say: “using flex utilities” 
 
   9. What is Navbar? 
     Answer: 
Navbar is a responsive navigation bar used for menus. 
 
   10. What is Modal? 
     Answer: 
Modal is a popup dialog box used for forms, alerts, etc. 
 
   11. What are utility classes? 
     Answer: 
Utility classes are predefined classes used for spacing, alignment, and colors. 
     Example: 
• mt-3 
• p-2 
• text-center 
 
   12. Bootstrap 5 features   
     Answer: 
Bootstrap 5 removed jQuery and uses pure JavaScript with improved performance. 
 
   13. What is offset? 
     Answer: 
Offset is used to create space before a column. 
 
   14. What is card? 
     Answer: 
Card is a flexible container used to display content like text, images, and buttons. 
 
   15. How Bootstrap makes responsive design? 
     Answer: 
Bootstrap uses grid system, breakpoints, and responsive utility classes to adjust layout 
for different screens. 
 
   QUICK PRACTICAL ANSWERS (IMPRESS INTERVIEWER) 
Create 2 equal columns 
<div class="col-6"></div> 
<div class="col-6"></div> 
3 equal columns 
<div class="col-4"></div> 
<div class="col-4"></div> 
<div class="col-4"></div> 
Responsive layout example 
<div class="col-sm-12 col-md-6 col-lg-4"></div> 
say: 
“Full width in mobile, half in tablet, 1/3 in desktop” 
Hide element in mobile 
d-none d-md-block 
Add spacing 
mt-3 p-2 
Align right 
d-flex justify-content-end 
• Grid (12 columns)    
• Breakpoints    
• Flex (d-flex)    
• Container    
• One example    
What are Bootstrap components? 
Answer: Pre-built UI elements like: 
• Navbar 
• Cards 
• Modals 
• Carousel 
• Buttons 
What is .img-fluid? 
Answer: It makes images responsive by applying max-width: 100% and auto height. 
How do you hide/show elements in Bootstrap? 
Answer: Using display utility classes. 
Example: 
HTML 
d-none d-md-block 
What is gutter in Bootstrap? 
Answer: Gutter is the space between columns, controlled using classes like g-3, gx
2, gy-4. 
What is mobile-first approach? 
Answer: Bootstrap follows a mobile-first approach, meaning styles are designed for 
mobile devices first and then extended for larger screens using breakpoints. 
Row and col 
• Row is used to create a horizontal layout 
• Columns are placed inside the row 
• Total columns in one row = 12 
Columns should always be inside a row, and row should be inside a container. 
Difference between Bootstrap and CSS? 
Answer: 
CSS is used to design from scratch, while Bootstrap provides pre-built classes and 
components for faster development. 
